R=[row('heading and first claim',r'old Prop uncertain; inserted Prop Soit X,Y; en uncertain; boundary dot/prime',r'Soient X,Y; clean heading; boundary dot',r'old Prop uncertain; inserted Prop Soit X,Y; en; boundary dot','The inserted verb is Soit with a single final t, followed by X,Y and the still-capitalized baseline Deux. En is readable; the mark above the closing parenthesis in the first box is a rounded dot. The older title remains blackened and uncertain.','020_top.jpg','misread word','high'),row('small upper-left note',r'partie de cancelled Th then th., both uncertain',r'omitted',r'C’s note and uncertainties retained','Partie de is clear, followed by overlapping tall strokes and a terminal point. The older and newer Th/th readings cannot safely be separated further.','020_title_margin.jpg','omission','medium',C=False),row('supremum assertion revision',r'live De plus; inserted X et Y ont une borne sup. dans/en; cancelled parmi toutes les parties; live l’ens ... ordonnées par l’inclusion; cancelled fermées modérées qui contient X',r'De struck; most revision flattened/unread; no complete order relation',r'C’s layers with cancelled parmi resolved; dans/en, toutes les and contient remain uncertain','De is written under the first box and plus starts the next baseline; neither is cancelled. The inserted line sits above the barred parmi ... parties. L’ens des parties modérées ordonnées par and l’inclusion remain live around the older cancelled clause.','020_top.jpg','deletion state','medium',marked=True),row('marginal proof indication',r'cancelled Dém uncertain; Sup/sup; question des frontières uncertain',r'fragmentary margin with convenons and modérée',r'cancelled D/Dém uncertain; Dém double récurrence sur nb de comp. conn. de X et de Y (pour l’existence du Sup et la question des frontières)','After rotation, double récurrence and the component-count phrase are fully readable. Sup begins with a larger capital S; question des frontières continues beneath the overlapping baseline deletion. The earlier crossed heading may be only a D-start and is marked accordingly.','020_margin1.jpg','readable ink left as \\ill{}','medium',marked=True),row('notation sentence',r'cancelled X et Y, et on; On écrit cette partie; On a',r'On note cette partie; et on a',r'C’s wording retained','The verb has the accented é and cr strokes of écrit. The second On begins with a capital and is not preceded by a live et. The preceding X et Y, et on lies under a single cancellation line.','020_top.jpg / 020_middle.jpg','misread word','high',C=False),row('marginal remark and separator',r'readable Rem note with tte and mod. doubtful; separator described in comment only',r'note omitted/unread',r'C’s note retained; two separating strokes drawn in TikZ','The note says that a moderate Z in relative moderate position with X and Y remains so with their intersection and moderated union. Its tte and short mod. remain visually compressed. Two parallel strokes separate this remark from the proof note and are now rendered rather than merely commented.','020_margin2.jpg','drawing or diagram','medium',marked=True),row('corollary',r'Cor; partie/parties; cancelled rel; ds/dans; ens',r'no Cor; live rel.; dans; ens.',r'Cor; parties; cancelled rel; dans; ens','Cor is separately underlined. The final s of parties is visible; rel is scribbled out. Dans has four connected strokes; ens has no added point. The intersection’s i index and all high boundary dots are visible in the displays.','020_middle.jpg / 020_bottom.jpg','deletion state','high'),row('warning about closure',r'quelc/seule; L/scr L; adh. and f. uncertain; set starts 0/1',r'NB and fragments only',r'Attention; quelc; cal L; adh.; f.; set starts 0; other wording retained','The heading is Attention, underlined. Quelc has a descending q followed by uelc, and the ground-set L is looped. The closure abbreviation has adh and a point; f. follows ens. The first number in the displayed set is a closed oval, 0. No closing parenthesis is supplied at the end of the note.','020_margin3.jpg','readable ink left as \\ill{}','high',marked=True),row('example’s last lines',r'prendre/quand; extra c/e before petit; cancelled et; qqconq; cancelled Et en ce =; b cancelled est comp.; inserted élément de L',r'prenant; no extra letter; unread cancellations; live Z; non comparable; cal L',r'C’s doubtful fragments and comp. retained; looped cal L in insertion','The small extra curl after plus is present and remains c/e. A separate qqconq-like group sits below the first line. The old words are barred; the two-stroke mark in that draft remains unsure equals, not a supplied live Z. Comp. is the live abbreviated word, with no preceding non. The inserted ground-set glyph has a calligraphic loop.','020_bottom.jpg','misread word','medium'),row('watermark','omitted','omitted',r'\unsure{ra Strong Extra}','Very pale outline lettering is retained only as an uncertain visible fragment; it is interrupted by the main writing.','020_watermark.jpg','omission','low')]
R[2]['consequential']='The assertion of a supremum is live; the cancellations affect earlier formulations around it, not the whole statement.'
save(20,t,R,[('text','top','Prop Soit X,Y'),('text','upper third','De plus'),('text','upper middle','On écrit cette partie'),('text','middle','Cor Soit'),('text','lower third','Ex'),('text','bottom','mais en général'),('text','paper background','ra Strong Extra')],['Upper note Th/th and old Prop retained uncertain. En and first boundary dot resolved.','Parmi resolved; toutes les, dans/en and contient remain uncertain. Old proof heading expanded to D/Dém as the visible surviving letter may be only the initial. Sup and question des frontières resolved.','Remark tte and mod. remain uncertain. Corollary parties and dans resolved.','Warning quelc, calligraphic L, adh., f. and initial 0 resolved.','Bottom prendre/quand, extra c/e, qqconq and all cancelled fragments retain their uncertainty. Final inserted L is looped and transcribed calligraphically.'],'Whole page, both halves and each slanted margin read. High dots in all three boundary displays are visible; the large finite-union dot is small but survives above the closing parenthesis.')
